-*   **Connectivity:** The standard Bresenham algorithm produces a 6-connected path in 3D (moving along one axis at a time, or diagonally across faces). A 26-connected path (allowing corner crossings) may miss intersections that a 6-connected path detects, but requires less computation [S5, unofficial]. The basic integer accumulation described above yields a path that is topologically consistent with the line segment but may not visit every voxel touched by the continuous ray if the ray passes through a voxel corner [S5, S12, unofficial].
